{"clock":32,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"a39d5427d18e28cd6dcf7a62ae6189549be9b408","forge_id":"5999844096","number":"46","url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/eesd-modern-masonry-walls-db/issues/46"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"a39d5427d18e28cd6dcf7a62ae6189549be9b408","field":"title","value":"[BUG](Header) The header takes a third of a phone screen"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"a39d5427d18e28cd6dcf7a62ae6189549be9b408","field":"body","value":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** on a phone the site header is 293 px tall, about a third of the screen. The five nav links wrap one per line, with the logo and the EESD link around them.\n- **Why:** the header's only narrow-screen rule is \"wrap\"; it has no phone layout.\n- **User impact:** on a 390 × 844 phone, the database table starts below the first third of the screen, on every page.\n- **Effort:** small\n\n---\n\n### What users experience\nAt 390 px wide the header measures 293 px; at 768 px and up it is 68 px. The nav links wrap onto separate lines with large gaps, the EPFL logo sits in the middle, and \"EESD ↗\" takes its own line.\n\n### What we propose\nBelow 40rem, a one-line bar of about 4rem: the EPFL logo on the left, a \"Menu\" button on the right. The button opens the five links as a list under the bar, with the lab link last. Wider screens keep today's header.\n\n### Done when\n- [ ] The header is at most about 4rem tall at 390 px.\n- [ ] The menu opens and closes by click and keyboard. It has `aria-expanded`, Escape closes it, and following a link closes it.\n- [ ] The current page is still marked in the menu.\n- [ ] No horizontal scroll at 390 px.\n\n### Technical notes\n`frontend/src/layouts/MainLayout.vue` holds the header: DS `epfl-header` classes, plus a `width \u003c= 64rem` rule that only wraps. Keep to DS tokens, with no hex and no px. Every new string goes in `en.json`.\n"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"a39d5427d18e28cd6dcf7a62ae6189549be9b408","field":"status","value":"open"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"d4dd02f9bf55c08ed70759b8926479f5b68e66a2","time":1793024757,"data":{"issue":"a39d5427d18e28cd6dcf7a62ae6189549be9b408","field":"labels","value":"bug"}}]}